  "result": "Shell completion now treats `#` as an ordinary character instead of cutting the command line off there. I ran `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` and all 68 tests pass. I didn't run the full suite.\n\n- **Fix:** in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), I set `lex.commenters = \"\"`, so `#` is no longer read as a comment. I also added a `versionchanged:: 8.5.1` note to the docstring.\n- **Tests:** I added three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `a#b`, a word starting with `#`, and `'a#b` with an unclosed quote.\n- **Changelog:** I added a `## Version 8.5.1` (Unreleased) entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n\nI skipped the optional extra test in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
